This script uploads a file to a folder on Google Drive. If the file can be
converted into the Google format, such as a Google Sheet, it will be converted.

Install PyDrive2 and enable the Drive API for your Google Cloud project.
Run from this example directory, with your desktop OAuth client configuration
saved as client_secrets.json. The script reads the adjacent settings.yaml
and saves user tokens in credentials.json in the working directory.

    python upload.py FOLDER_ID /path/to/report.csv

On the first run, open the printed URL in a browser that can reach the local
callback. Choose a destination folder accessible to this app and user with
the configured drive.file scope. A new CSV is imported as a Google Sheet
when Drive advertises that import format. One existing file visible to the app with the
same name is updated. Multiple matches stop the upload.

This example is adapted from Evren Yurtesen (https://github.com/yurtesen/)
with his consent.
Originally posted here: https://github.com/prasmussen/gdrive/issues/154
